        "subject": "LU-20411 ksocklnd: annotate functions that hold global spinlocks",
        "message": "LU-20411 ksocklnd: annotate functions that hold global spinlocks\n\nClang 22 with kernel 7.1 can statically enforce locking\nannotations like __must_hold(). Fix violations for the\nksocknal_data.ksnd_connd_lock and ksocknal_data.ksnd_global_lock\nby adding annotations to functions that omit them. This fixes\nvarious -Wthread-safety-analysis warnings.\n\nThe shared (read-side) annotations such as __must_hold_shared()\nonly exist since Linux v7.0. Add a lustre_compat shadow header\nthat defines them away on older kernels.\n\n[1] https://docs.kernel.org/dev-tools/context-analysis.html\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Timothy Day <timday@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I2413811657e65a2880fad0e30d9d35805c0a4310\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
